<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery gut looping morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Functions document the inertia and cube-root scaling formulas (L35-44), but lack explicit mappings to Savin et al. (2011) Figs. 1-4, Supplementary Sec. S2-S4, Nerurkar et al. (2017) PNAS Fig. 2-4, and the 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_062_gut_looping_differential_growth.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L35–L65: Brief docstrings without explicit paper figure/section or Lean 4 theorem cross-references <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L35-L65>" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery gut looping morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Computes the exact annular second moment of area I_t = (pi/4)*(R_t^4 - R_i^4) and cube-root scaling length ell_* = (E_t*I_t / (E_m*h_m))^(1/3) (L35-43), backed by 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_062_gut_looping_differential_growth.lean`. However, `generate_parametric_gut_curve` (L46-65) prescribes a hardcoded 3D sinusoid rather than minimizing the coupled Kirchhoff rod bending + axial stretching + neo-Hookean mesenteric traction energy functional, and no negative ablation control (surgical mesentery dissection / epsilon = 0) is simulated." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L46–L65: Parametric sinusoidal curve instead of discrete Kirchhoff rod + neo-Hookean mesentery energy minimization <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L46-L65>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery gut looping morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 56/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L205-238) reports Chick E12 predicted vs observed wavelength and radius plus Chick E8-E16 Pearson r and RMSE, but does not measure physical rod curvature kappa(s) or zero-crossing loop wavelength from a relaxed 3D Kirchhoff rod, does not evaluate cross-species collapse statistics across all 14 vertebrate data points, and extracts zero computer-vision metrics from the specimen image." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L205–L238: Only 3 analytical Chick metrics returned in measure_morphoeval() without 3D rod curvature or specimen CV metrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L205-L238>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e12-predicted-gut-loop-radius-of-curvature-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e12-predicted-gut-loop-wavelength-lambda>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e8-e16-wavelength-scaling-pearson-r> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery gut looping morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 54.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py` (overall weighted score: 56.4/100). The v1 script implements Savin et al.'s (2011) annular tube inertia I_t = (pi/4)*(R_t^4 - R_i^4), characteristic length scale ell_* = (E_t*I_t / (E_m*h_m))^(1/3), and Chick E8-E16 wavelength/radius scaling, but uses a synthetic sinusoidal 3D curve rather than minimizing a discrete Kirchhoff elastic rod + neo-Hookean mesentery energy functional, omits the 4-species comparative collapse (zebra finch, quail, chick, mouse) and BMP2/Noggin/surgical-ablation controls, and does not segment the vendored biological mesentery/intestine specimen image. Overall 54.5/100 (faithfulness 47.9, reproducibility 70.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 48, Morphometric validation 56, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/gut_looping_differential_growth_comparison.png: rendered output of 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py at 8871db0, image/png, 242127 B, 1413×1054 px, artifact_sha256 a509fa903edf6a286172076d79d801863c3bac04a90bdbc10f3298cd0a884e04 (sha256 a509fa903edf6a286172076d79d801863c3bac04a90bdbc10f3298cd0a884e04), spec_fingerprint 643f6989deff1f1d47f576fe1e43c257f747c5e39321e10638b972d0ac0dc491. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 643f6989deff1f1d47f576fe1e43c257f747c5e39321e10638b972d0ac0dc491; artifact_sha256: a509fa903edf6a286172076d79d801863c3bac04a90bdbc10f3298cd0a884e04; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json=f73121bb4140187f..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/intestine_mesentery_specimen.jpg=e12fee9ac1fb5f3d..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/paper_citations.bib=21703c48df51dd52..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/scout_manifest.json=0723b42b4d825087...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add runtime SHA-256 verification of all 4 files in `datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/`, expose full CLI parameters (`--epsilon`, `--E-ratio`, `--R-t`, `--h-m`, `--seed`), and expand `self_test()` and `measure_morphoeval()` to cover all physical, cross-species, ablation, and specimen metrics.",
        "remediation needed: Evaluate the full 14-point cross-species scaling collapse across Zebra finch (Taeniopygia guttata), Quail (Coturnix japonica), Chick (Gallus gallus), and Mouse (Mus musculus) (Savin et al. 2011 Fig. 4e-f) alongside Nerurkar et al. (2017) PNAS BMP2 gain-of-function, Noggin loss-of-function, and surgical mesentery ablation (epsilon = 0) negative controls.",
        "remediation needed: Implement computer-vision segmentation of `datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/intestine_mesentery_specimen.jpg` to segment the yellow-orange dorsal mesentery fan and pinkish-red intestinal loop ridges, quantifying empirical inter-loop spacing, CV, and loop count.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the synthetic sinusoidal curve with a genuine 3D discrete Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery energy minimizer (L-BFGS-B relaxation of axial stretching + bending + mesenteric radial sheet traction + steric repulsion) and extract emergent loop wavelength, curvature kappa(s), and tortuosity directly from the relaxed 3D centerline." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.45e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) Kirchhoff elastic rod + stretched neo-Hookean dorsal mesentery gut looping morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 48/100" ;
